# Single Source Of Truth Enforcement

## Goal
- Prevent duplicated runtime configuration across DB tables, APIs, services, and UI state.

## Non-negotiables
- A setting has exactly one authoritative persistence location.
- A setting has exactly one canonical API contract.
- A setting is editable in exactly one UI surface; all other appearances must be read-only summaries.

## Runtime settings this applies to
- LLM model and provider settings
- guardrails and policy behavior
- KnowledgeBase binding and retrieval behavior
- tool allow/deny policy

## Required pattern
- If agents need runtime behavior, they should reference one canonical profile/policy object rather than carrying duplicated copies.
- Do not add shadow fields, sync code, or “convenience copies” of the same setting.

## Before adding a setting
1. Identify the single owner.
2. Identify the single API that exposes it.
3. Identify the single UI editor for it.
4. Explain how all other code reads it by reference.

If you cannot answer all four, stop and redesign before coding.
